      {
        "TOCHeading": "Abstract",
        "Description": "Abstract of this patent.",
        "Information": [
          {
            "ReferenceNumber": 1,
            "Name": "Abstract",
            "Value": {
              "StringWithMarkup": [
                {
                  "String": "[Translated] Process and means such as a compartment device or distribution assembly or transdermal device comprising backing layers (2), drug formulation (4), permeation enhancer formulation (6), membrane for pressure break (8) ) diffusion membrane (10), adhesive (12), and release coating (14), to improve the epidermal, transdermal, and dermal permeability of a pharmacologically active agent, topically applied (e.g., a drug or medicine such as: steroid, aspirin, phenyl butazone, enzyme inhibitor, among others), which has a low rate of penetration into the skin in the absence of a permeation enhancer and which is unstable and degraded during long-term storage with the particular permeability (such as: alcohols, fatty alcohols and their esters, among others). A first composition containing a drug, a salt thereof, a chemical derivative or formulation thereof in a dermatologically acceptable vehicle and a second composition containing a permeability enhancer of an acceptable vehicle. The compositions are physically separated up to application to a body or face surface and are topically applicable, either at the same time or sequentially over the course of a short period of time to each other, and mixed or combined to form a final active composition. on the skin. It allows a quantity of therapeutically effective drug to be delivered to the skin and to the systematic circulation, by the action of the permeation improver in the compositional agent at the point of use."
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
